<task id="086" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rate card and rate join the secure family; each row gets its own owner; the rate card workbook is filed under its record (uac-r2 review item 5, round 2 items 086.1-086.8, D-145, D-146)</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172, D-141, D-145, D-146), wave W3-10</phase>
    <gate>081 and 085 done; sprk_createdbyperson on sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate live on dev (080); UAC T7 merged to master; owner OK for the live refusal probes and the two -Apply runs on dev; uac-r2 reviews every edit to its files</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Record ownership on Secure records (a Secure-scoped import is refused today; a later Secure is never followed), uac-r2's lineage, resolver, role, census, depth-assertion and client files, the workbook document's filing and external visibility, and live role and schema writes on dev: tenant-isolation code.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-relevant ownership change across uac-r2-owned files with a binding review, mirroring 081's secure-family change for a second pair of tables.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the same uac-r2 files and shared guards as 081 (SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 and its Pester pin, SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs, bffChildWriteAdapter.ts, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests) and RateCardImportService.cs after 085. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>081, 085</deps>
    <tags>bff, security, tenant-isolation, testing, rules</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Put sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate in the secure family in ONE change, as 081 does for sprk_ruleset (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 5.4, revised by uac-r2's round 2): lineage entries, sprk_ratecard in OwnershipParentEntities and in the client OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES list, role rows with live refusal probes applied before the BFF deploy, the creator-person stamp and script entries (secure and verify only; 080 created the column), census ChildTables / Routed entries / PersonBearingWriters, and a separate non-throwing NFR-05 list for both. In RateCardImportService, take each row's owner parents from its own lookups (card → core record, rate → card), resolving once per distinct parent set; give new firm-level timekeeper rows their own no-parent owner, never the matter's; and file the workbook document under the card's core record, Restricted, owned from its own row and stored in the record's container (D-145). Count cards already on Secure records before deploy and reconcile them after. Core-record delete always keeps the card, unlinked (D-146); this task adds no delete code.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IRecordOwnershipResolver, SecureChildReconciler, the uac-r2 secure-family guards and the rate card import (078).</role>

  <goal>A rate card import scoped to a Secure matter succeeds, its card and rates owned by the Secure team; making a matter Secure later re-owns its card and rates through the reconciler (and Unsecure moves them back); cards already on Secure records before the deploy are counted and re-owned by one reconcile run after it; new timekeeper rows are owned by the caller's business-unit team whatever the card's scope; a record-scoped card's workbook is filed under its record, Restricted and owned from its own row; SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests, the census, the Pester pin and the creator-person agreement test pass with both tables; the NFR-05 run reports no non-admin role reaching the Secure business unit on either table, and a missing privilege name never blinds the census.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note sections 5.4 and 12 (uac-r2 review item 5; round 2 items 086.1-086.8). Decisions: D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q8 direct inheritance is a read rule), D-141, D-145 (source documents), D-146 (core-record delete always keeps the card, unlinked; supersedes D-120's "deleted with its record" and D-141 Q10). Cite symbols, not line numbers (uac-r2 round 2, general). The gap, by symbol: RateCardImportService.ImportAsync resolves ONE owner from the core record and applies it to the timekeeper rows, the card and the rates, and passes it to the workbook document; the per-row writes go through its WriteAsync helper; neither sprk_ratecard nor sprk_ratecardrate is in SecureChildLineage, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES or the census (RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests has no RateCardImportService entry). Entity sets: sprk_ratecards, sprk_ratecardrates (docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md). sprk_ratecardrate.sprk_ratecard is parental (cascade assign). Spaarke Basic User and Core User hold prvReadsprk_ratecard and prvReadsprk_ratecardrate at Deep (SpaarkeMaster Roles). This task calls no ReparentAsync: an import only creates rows; a later Secure or Unsecure moves them through the reconciler. Cards can also be created on the model-driven form, outside the BFF: such a card is owned by its creator until the reconciler re-owns it. UAC T7 (notes/2119-manage-access-all-forms-design.md §6 on work/unified-access-control-r2; owner accepted D7 in UAC round 110): every external document surface hides a document whose own sprk_accesspermission is Restricted. uac-r2's delete design: projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/core-record-delete-design.md §12 (3fbf650fb): the delete job always unlinks R's own rate card (with its rates) and never deletes or re-owns it. The 081 change is the reference for every file touched.</background>
