  <constraints>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 round 2, general">Step 0 merges origin/master into the branch (including uac-r2 #2150 once it lands) before any edit. Cite symbols, not line numbers. Every edit to a uac-r2 file ships in this task's PR and is reviewed by uac-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 5, round 2 items 086.1-086.3, design note 5.4">ONE change carries every part: SecureChildLineage T("sprk_ratecard", "sprk_ratecards", ("sprk_matter", Matter), ("sprk_project", Project), ("sprk_workassignment", WorkAssignment)) and T("sprk_ratecardrate", "sprk_ratecardrates", ("sprk_ratecard", "sprk_ratecard")); "sprk_ratecard" in OwnershipParentEntities (the parent of its rates; sprk_ratecardrate is a lineage child only); sprk_ratecard (NOT sprk_ratecardrate) in OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES in bffChildWriteAdapter.ts, so SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests holds; role rows for both (kind child, Read, Basic, reason, verbatim probe evidence); both in RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and in Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 under $SolutionHomes (the script secures and verifies; 080 created the column), with tests/scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.Tests.ps1 updated in the same change; census ChildTables, Routed entries for the RateCardImportService card and rate creates, and a PersonBearingWriters entry naming the method that writes ("RateCardImportService.cs", "WriteAsync", the admin who imported); the NFR-05 entries for both tables (below).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 round 2 item 086.2 (MUST, as 081.1)">Do NOT append the two tables to SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.GuardedPrivileges (RequireGuardedPrivilegesResolved throws the census away on a missing name). Add them to the separate, non-throwing list 081 created, graded by clause 1, where an unresolved name becomes a finding naming it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 4, round 2 item 086.6">Each row's owner parents come from its own lookups through RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(row): the card from its core lookup (none for a Firm card), each rate from its sprk_ratecard. ResolveOwnerAsync(ForParents(..., caller) with { RequestedBy = caller }), resolved ONCE per distinct parent set per import (the card's set once; every rate of one card shares [card], so once), never once per row. A refusal writes nothing (the existing OwnerRefused outcome).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 5 (timekeepers)">New sprk_timekeeper rows are firm-level: their owner is a NO-PARENT resolution (the caller's business-unit team, RequestedBy = caller), resolved once per import and never the card's owner, whatever the card's scope. Existing roster rows the import reuses are not touched. sprk_timekeeper does not join the secure family.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-145, uac-r2 round 2 item 086.4 (MUST) and its D7 / T7 update">The workbook document (created through the CreateDocumentAsync seam): a Firm or ClientDefault card's workbook stays unlinked in the Procedure Library, owned by the caller's business-unit team with no parent; a Record-scoped card's workbook is FILED under the card's core record through the document's own typed lookup, owned from its OWN row (ResolveOwnerAsync(ForParents(ParentsOf(docRow))) with RequestedBy = caller; never the card's owner handed over), stored in that record's container (RecordContainerResolver), and created with its own sprk_accesspermission = Restricted (option value read live), so UAC T7 hides it from every external document surface. The old behaviour (unlinked, carrying the card's owner) is removed, not kept as a fallback. The census UnscannedWriters gains a row for RateCardImportService as a CreateDocumentAsync seam caller.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 round 2 item 086.5 (SHOULD)">Before the first deploy of a BFF carrying this code to an environment, count the cards (and their rates) already on Secure records there (read-only, recorded in the notes); after the role rows and the BFF are live, run the reconcile once (the SecureChildReconciler sweep or Make Secure's Step 8 path, as uac-r2 names) and record that the count of cards on Secure records not owned by the Secure team is 0.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 round 2 item 086.8 (NOTE)">This task calls no ReparentAsync, so the #2150 conditional-reparent contract does not apply to it; its creates still handle a resolver refusal (nothing written, ProblemDetailsHelper.RecordOwnerRefused, a test pins it). A card created on the form (outside the BFF) under a Secure record is owned by its creator until the reconciler re-owns it: read the reconciler's interval from configuration and state that window in the notes and in design note 5.4.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (live part, as 081), round 2 item 086.7">Live refusal probes on dev, one per table, before the privileges are added (verbatim 0x80040299 into the evidence); then Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -WhatIf / -Apply / -Verify and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 dry run / -Apply / -Verify, each with the owner's OK. Both -Verify runs gate EVERY target environment before a BFF carrying this code deploys there (079 for dev, the release path for any other).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (NFR-05)">The depth check covers sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate for every non-admin role; record the live NFR-05 result on dev.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-146, uac-r2 core-record-delete-design.md §12 (3fbf650fb)">No delete code and no delete-Restrict. Core-record delete ALWAYS keeps the record's own card (with its rates), clears its core lookup and never deletes it; the card then applies to nothing (S2). The delete job never re-owns: a card under a Secure matter stays Secure-owned after the unlink, reachable only by the Secure team or an admin; retire or re-scope of such an orphan is a known limit (design note 4.5), not this task's work. Q8 is unchanged: a matter's card judges its direct children's invoices app-only; joining the secure family changes who can READ the card, not which invoices it judges.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: no new service or registration; publish-size delta; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

