  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">git fetch; git merge origin/master (including #2150 when it lands); confirm 081, 085 and UAC T7 are ancestors of HEAD (STOP if T7 is missing); confirm sprk_createdbyperson exists on both tables (metadata read); read notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md.</step>
    <step order="1">RateCardImportService: parents from each row's own lookups, resolved once per distinct parent set; the timekeeper owner as a separate no-parent resolution; tests (Secure-scoped import, Firm import, timekeeper owner under a Secure-scoped import, resolver call counts, refusal writes nothing).</step>
    <step order="2">The workbook document (D-145): unlinked for Firm / ClientDefault; filed, own-row owner, record container, Restricted for Record; census UnscannedWriters row; tests.</step>
    <step order="3">Secure family in one change: lineage, OwnershipParentEntities, OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES (card only), StampedChildTables + script ($SolutionHomes) + Pester pin, role rows, census (ChildTables, Routed, PersonBearingWriters on WriteAsync), the separate NFR-05 list; SecureChildLineageTests, SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests, the reconciler test (card and rates re-owned on secure and unsecure).</step>
    <step order="4">Read the reconciler's interval from configuration; record the form-created-card window (086.8).</step>
    <step order="5">With the owner's OK: the probes, both -Apply runs with -Verify, the pre-deploy count of cards on Secure records, the live NFR-05 run. After 079's deploy: the reconcile run and the zero count. Notices to uac-r2 before and after.</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build; dotnet test (unit, ArchTests, the data-mutation agreement test); the Pester pin; the client package test that holds OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES; publish-size delta; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="7">Review: uac-r2. Record it.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/086-ratecard-secure-family.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any part of the secure-family change cannot land in the same PR as the others, STOP (a subset fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests or the census).</trigger>
    <trigger>If UAC T7 has not merged, STOP: a filed workbook on a matter with partner grants would be visible to those partners (D-145).</trigger>
    <trigger>If sprk_createdbyperson is missing on sprk_ratecard or sprk_ratecardrate, STOP (080 creates it; uac-r2's script never does for a $SolutionHomes table).</trigger>
    <trigger>If a probe's create SUCCEEDS, delete the probe row, record it and STOP; ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the live NFR-05 run reports a non-admin role whose Read on sprk_ratecard or sprk_ratecardrate reaches the Secure business unit, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the post-deploy reconcile leaves any card on a Secure record not owned by the Secure team, STOP and report to uac-r2 and the main session.</trigger>
    <trigger>If routing needs a resolver change beyond adding sprk_ratecard to OwnershipParentEntities, STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The cards, rates and import exist (017, 078); the secure-family lists and guards exist and already take sprk_ruleset (081), including the separate NFR-05 list and the source-document filing; the resolver already routes the card's owner. Grep finds sprk_ratecard in none of SecureChildLineage, the role JSON, StampedChildTables, OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES or the census.</existing>
    <extension>Only existing lists, guards and the import are extended; no new service, registration, table or endpoint. Two new list entries per guard plus one reconciler test file.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A rate card import scoped to a Secure matter is refused by Dataverse (0x80040299); a card on a matter made Secure later stays readable outside the wall; a Secure matter's import hides new firm timekeepers from the firm's ordinary readers; and the workbook of a matter's card sits outside the record and outside the wall.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1, Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (owner OK); Invoke-Pester for the script pin</tool>
    <tool name="npm">the Spaarke.UI.Components test that holds OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">probes (owner OK), role and metadata reads, the card counts</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">RateCardImportService.cs, SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs, bffChildWriteAdapter.ts, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">the test files listed in relevant-files, including tests/scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.Tests.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/086-ratecard-secure-family.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An import scoped to a Secure matter resolves the Secure team as owner of the card and every rate, and creates them (unit test with the resolver; the live probe shows the role row is what makes Dataverse accept it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner parents: the card passes exactly [core record] (none for a Firm card); each rate's parents == [the card] (negative: never [core record]); an import of one card with N rates calls the resolver exactly once for the card, once for the rates and once for the timekeepers (negative: not N times).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Timekeepers: under a Secure-scoped import a new timekeeper row is owned by the caller's business-unit team (no parents), not the Secure team (negative); a reused roster row is not written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Workbook (D-145): a Firm card's workbook has no core lookup, lives in the Procedure Library and is owned by the caller's business-unit team; a Record card's workbook carries exactly the card's core record in its typed lookup, its owner resolution is called with exactly [that record] from the document row (negative: never the card's owner handed over), its file goes to the record's container (negative: never the Procedure Library), and its sprk_accesspermission is Restricted; the census lists RateCardImportService in UnscannedWriters as a seam caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The reconciler test re-owns a matter's card and its rates when the matter is made Secure, and moves them back on Unsecure; a Firm card (no lookup) is never reached (negative).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests (sprk_ratecard in OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES; negative: sprk_ratecardrate not in it), EveryChildTableTheServerCreatesCarriesTheCreatorPersonColumn, EveryAppCreateWriterThatActsForAPersonNamesThem (the PersonBearingWriters entry names WriteAsync), EveryRoutedEntryRoutesThroughTheResolver, ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests and the Pester pin pass with both tables, each a $SolutionHomes table; removing either table from the role JSON fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-05: GuardedPrivileges is unchanged; the separate list covers both tables; a census read missing prvReadsprk_ratecardrate still grades and reports exactly one finding naming it (negative: the census is not thrown away); the live NFR-05 run on dev is recorded with no finding on them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notes record both probes' verbatim refusals, the -Apply / -Verify outputs, the owner's OK with dates, the pre-deploy count of cards on Secure records, the post-reconcile zero count, and the form-created-card window with the reconciler interval read from configuration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No delete code, no delete-Restrict and no Retire logic is added (negative); the notes record that the delete job keeps and unlinks the card and never re-owns it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta recorded; no package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>A task of its own (design note 5.4): 085 is a resolver change that runs beside 083 (p-safe true); this one edits uac-r2's shared files after 081, needs live probes and uac-r2's review, and follows 085 on RateCardImportService.cs. Two adversarial passes (tenant-isolation). D-146: Secure-owned orphan cards after a core-record delete are reachable only by the Secure team or an admin; retire / re-scope of them by billing admins is a known limit, not R1 work.</notes>

